SUMMARY:Sammy Obeid LIVE at Pittsburgh Improv
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nSammy Obeid is a Lebanese-Palestinian American comedian born in Oakland\, California\, who double-majored in Business and Mathematics at UC Berkeley — and then turned down a job at Google to pursue stand-up comedy. That decision paid off in a big way. \nObeid is best known as the host of 100 Humans on Netflix\, and has appeared on NBC’s Last Comic Standing\, America’s Got Talent\, and TBS’s Conan. He holds a world record for performing stand-up comedy 1\,001 nights in a row — a remarkable feat that was featured in both Time Magazine and The New York Times. \nSammy’s comedy is smart\, sharp\, and deeply personal — blending his unique background in math and business with relatable observations about life\, culture\, and the human experience. His shows are known for being intellectually engaging while remaining laugh-out-loud funny from start to finish. \nEvent Details\nDate: Tuesday\, July 21\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM (Doors open at 5:30 PM) \nVenue: Pittsburgh Improv\, 166 E. Bridge St\, Homestead\, PA 15120 \nAge Restriction: Ages 21 and up \nNote: This is a one-night-only special event at the Pittsburgh Improv. \nAbout the Venue\nThe Pittsburgh Improv is located at 166 E. Bridge Street in Homestead\, PA — just minutes from downtown Pittsburgh. As part of the nationally recognized Improv Comedy Club chain\, the Pittsburgh Improv is one of the premier comedy venues in the region. \nThe club features a full-service restaurant and bar\, making it a perfect destination for a complete night out. The intimate showroom seats approximately 300 guests\, ensuring every seat has a great sightline to the stage. The venue’s warm\, welcoming atmosphere is ideal for the kind of thoughtful\, engaging comedy that Sammy Obeid delivers. \nParking is available nearby\, and the venue is easily accessible from major highways. The Pittsburgh Improv consistently brings top national touring comedians to the Pittsburgh area\, and Sammy Obeid is a standout addition to their summer 2026 lineup. \nWhat to Expect\nSammy Obeid delivers a stand-up performance that is as smart as it is funny. Expect sharp observations\, personal storytelling\, and a comedian who can make complex ideas hilarious. This is a solo stand-up show — expect 60–75 minutes of intelligent\, engaging comedy. \nSammy’s unique background — from UC Berkeley math major to Netflix host to world record holder — gives him a perspective unlike any other comedian working today. His shows are perfect for fans who love comedy that makes you think as much as it makes you laugh. \nPlease note: This is an ages 21 and up event. Valid ID is required at the door. Third-party tickets will not be honored — purchase only from authorized sellers. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $25 – $50 (plus fees) \nTickets are available through official channels and resale marketplaces. This is a one-night-only show\, so purchase early to secure your spot! \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/sammy-obeid-live-at-pittsburgh-improv/
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Improv\, 166 E. Bridge St\, Homestead\, Pennsylvania\, 15120\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://i.ticketweb.com/i/00/08/98/03/51/Original.jpg
