SUMMARY:Martin Amini LIVE at Saint Andrew's Hall
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nMartin Amini is a rising star in stand-up comedy — a sharp\, relatable\, and wildly funny comedian based in Washington\, D.C.\, who has been selling out clubs and theaters across the country on his “I’m Not Toxic\, I’m Healing” Tour. \nBorn and raised in Silver Spring\, Maryland\, Martin draws his comedic inspiration from his uniquely diverse heritage — an Iranian father and a Bolivian mother — crafting a blend of humor that resonates with audiences of all backgrounds. His multicultural upbringing gives him a perspective that is both deeply personal and universally hilarious. \nBeyond his heritage\, Martin mines his own experiences of marriage and relationships for comedy gold\, delivering hilarious commentary on love\, commitment\, and the everyday chaos of modern life. He is also the founder of Room 808\, a comedian-run comedy club in Washington\, D.C.\, and is currently on a multi-continent tour showcasing his distinctive brand of stand-up to audiences worldwide. \nKnown for his sharp wit\, storytelling ability\, and crowd work\, Martin Amini is one of the most exciting live performers on the comedy circuit today. His Detroit stop at Saint Andrew’s Hall is not to be missed. \nEvent Details\nDate: Wednesday\, July 22\, 2026 \nTime: 7:30 PM EDT \nVenue: Saint Andrew’s Hall — 431 E Congress St\, Detroit\, MI 48226 \nPhone: (313) 961-8961 \nAge Restriction: 18+ (Fast Lane Access add-on available for eligible guests) \nContent: Stand-up comedy — adult themes and language expected. \nAbout the Venue\nSaint Andrew’s Hall is one of Detroit’s most storied and beloved live entertainment venues\, located at 431 E Congress St in the heart of downtown Detroit. With a capacity of approximately 1\,000\, Saint Andrew’s Hall offers an intimate\, high-energy atmosphere that makes every show feel electric and up-close. \nOriginally built as a Scottish fraternal hall in 1907\, the venue has been a cornerstone of Detroit’s live music and comedy scene for decades. Its exposed brick walls\, balcony seating\, and general admission floor create a raw\, authentic vibe that perfectly suits the energy of a live stand-up comedy performance. \nThe venue features a full bar\, excellent sightlines from both the floor and balcony\, and a sound system that ensures every punchline lands perfectly. Parking is available in nearby lots and structures throughout downtown Detroit. Saint Andrew’s Hall is easily accessible and centrally located\, making it a perfect destination for a night out in the city. \nWhat to Expect\nExpect a high-energy\, laugh-packed evening of stand-up comedy from one of the hottest touring comedians in the country. Martin Amini’s shows are known for their incredible crowd work\, sharp storytelling\, and the kind of relatable humor that has audiences in stitches from start to finish. \nThis is a solo stand-up performance in an intimate venue setting — meaning you’ll be close to the stage and fully immersed in the experience. Martin’s ability to read a room and connect with his audience in real time makes every show feel unique and spontaneous. \nDoors typically open before showtime. Arrive early to grab a drink at the bar and secure a great spot on the floor or in the balcony. This is an 18+ event — bring your valid photo ID. Fast Lane Access add-ons are available for those who want priority entry. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $46 – $65 (prices may vary based on seat selection and demand) \nTickets are on sale now. Martin Amini’s shows have been selling out across the country — don’t wait to grab yours for Detroit. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/martin-amini-live-at-saint-andrews-hall-detroit/
LOCATION:Saint Andrew’s Hall\, 431 E Congress St\, Detroit\, MI\, 48226\, USA
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.leadconnectorhq.com/image/f_webp/q_80/r_1200/u_https://assets.cdn.filesafe.space/l6OJNPCCOIt9XXD2MhmF/media/68d9e0eb373f4ec559447495.webp
